Read AGENTS.md at the repo root first. It is the canonical rules file for this project.

AGENTS.md holds the stack facts, architecture invariants, standing behavioral rules,
model/tool routing, and what's off-limits. docs/architecture.md is the deep reference.
Everything below is Cursor-specific and additive — it never overrides AGENTS.md.

## Cursor (Fable) notes

- Cursor is used primarily for cross-file refactors.
- Do not rewrite or output entire files — make targeted, namespaced edits and show the diff
  before applying.
- Never move Rapier physics or collision logic server-side; the server (party/index.ts)
  never simulates physics. Real-time host transforms, client input, and spill events go
  peer-to-peer over WebRTC DataChannels (src/netcode/p2p.js), not through the WebSocket.
- All color logic uses CART_COLORS in src/config.js — do not modify that object or the
  traverse material logic.
- index.html is the canonical menu markup; cart-rave-menu.html is deleted — do not recreate it.
